{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>Six days shall work be done.</b> And another verse says: ״ששת ימים תעבוד״ (Six days you shall labor). This is to say: when you do the will of the Omnipresent, your work is done by others — your slaves and your maidservants; and when you do not do His will, ״תעבוד״ — you yourself shall labor and you yourself shall do your own work. <b>Six days shall work be done.</b> Scripture restated it because of ״מות יומת״ (shall surely be put to death)."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:01:22.902127687Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}